{
  "_id": "28NgMpMQkmTy4uyFhPj8z4XVqml",
  "_type": "Docs",
  "_index": "a6",
  "title": "Deploying",
  "navigationTitle": "",
  "body": [
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Deploying an Alinea site means deploying your Next.js app. In production the dashboard is served by your site on `/admin`, and your handler route saves the editors' changes as commits to your git repository. To do that it needs a backend that signs users in and talks to your repository: "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Alinea Cloud",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "3JkF1r7nnTva2UpULvoNCkcsLLt",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "c1qjY2L4hq8JWfscRb_dD"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": " or "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "your own",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "3JkF1mPLVsh2IT1e6bucQSjdKMl",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "2YlEGKqhO4mqRqEwQexeqRI8Jfu"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Prepare your project"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "prepare-your-project"
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Config"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "config"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Tell Alinea where your site lives, where the handler is and on which path the dashboard is served, in your "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "CMS config",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "2YlC927lwX5hfm2G9JHx9j3yRux",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "259Ey7LXgqL7ZDGJ8XK1vBJmZrh"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": ":"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "CodeBlock",
      "_id": "2YlDwmJLzaL93bp5gYZmshbJG1P",
      "code": "import {createCMS} from 'alinea/next'\n\nexport const cms = createCMS({\n  // schema and workspaces ...\n  baseUrl: {\n    development: 'http://localhost:3000',\n    production: 'https://example.com'\n  },\n  handlerUrl: '/api/cms',\n  adminPath: '/admin'\n})",
      "fileName": "cms.ts",
      "language": "tsx",
      "compact": false
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`baseUrl.production` is required: the handler URL is resolved against it. Your config is also bundled into the dashboard, where only environment variables starting with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` or `PUBLIC_` exist. Use one of those if you read the URL from the environment, for example `production: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Build scripts"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "build-scripts"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Run Next.js through the Alinea CLI. `alinea build` bundles your content, generates the dashboard and then runs the command after `--`:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "CodeBlock",
      "_id": "3JkF1lXxItNfgDiKYvIlkabtjbu",
      "code": "{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"alinea dev -- next dev\",\n    \"build\": \"alinea build -- next build\",\n    \"start\": \"next start\"\n  }\n}",
      "fileName": "package.json",
      "language": "json"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Wrap your Next.js config in `withAlinea` from `alinea/next`. It serves the dashboard on `adminPath`, routes media URLs (`/admin/file/...`) to your handler and allows them in `next/image`:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "CodeBlock",
      "_id": "3JkF1r3TiOnjoSX7uCyFlp81Dob",
      "code": "import {withAlinea} from 'alinea/next'\n\nexport default withAlinea({\n  // your Next.js config\n})",
      "fileName": "next.config.ts",
      "language": "tsx"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "The build writes the dashboard to your public folder: an `admin.html` file and an `admin` folder with its assets, named after `adminPath`. They are generated on every build, so leave them out of git:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "CodeBlock",
      "_id": "2eM0q5z6cky9xrlPsHoH5ltj1A6",
      "code": "/public/admin*",
      "fileName": ".gitignore",
      "language": "text"
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "The handler route"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "the-handler-route"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "The route you created with `alinea init` handles every request of the dashboard:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "CodeBlock",
      "_id": "3JkF1rIUeY1i6uvhRoDhIEQmyCg",
      "code": "import {cms} from '@/cms'\nimport {createHandler} from 'alinea/next'\n\nconst handler = createHandler({cms})\n\nexport const GET = handler\nexport const POST = handler",
      "fileName": "app/(alinea)/api/cms/route.ts",
      "language": "tsx"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Without a `backend` option the handler connects to Alinea Cloud. Pass `backend` to "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "host it yourself",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "3JkF1rjlrxE2zflfbm3fdizSUyQ",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "2YlEGKqhO4mqRqEwQexeqRI8Jfu"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": ". Use the `afterCommit` hook to revalidate pages after editors publish, see "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Instant publishing",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "3JkF1meS2ymkPkPGboBxhScBPGH",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "3JjNWhIOOARLjiO2HjeVoVyVN48"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Hosting requirements"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "hosting-requirements"
    },
    {
      "_type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Node.js 24 or higher",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "_type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": " where your site runs, not only where it builds: the bundled content database is opened with Node's built-in SQLite."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "The Node.js runtime",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "_type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": " for the handler route. The handler refuses to run on the Edge runtime."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Server rendering.",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "_type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": " The handler is an API route, so a static export (`output: 'export'`) can't run the dashboard or serve media."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Deploy"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "deploy"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Push your code and deploy it as usual. Then open `/admin` on your deployed site:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "bulletList",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "Without a backend, the dashboard walks you through connecting the site to Alinea Cloud."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "listItem",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "_type": "text",
                  "text": "With a self-hosted backend, editors sign in with the method you configured."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "After the first publish, check that the change shows up on your site and that a commit appeared in your repository."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "ChapterLinkBlock",
      "_id": "3JkF1qrP1ACUJVy6B23JU2PwROo",
      "link": {
        "description": "Connect your site to a hosted backend in a few clicks.",
        "_id": "3JkF1qCQi9hbfsJFmyLcBFGWOGR",
        "_type": "entry",
        "_entry": "c1qjY2L4hq8JWfscRb_dD"
      }
    },
    {
      "_type": "ChapterLinkBlock",
      "_id": "3JkF1kRE16UIxZ5k3hNSJglMxbV",
      "link": {
        "description": "Run the backend yourself with your own database, auth and storage.",
        "_id": "3JkF1kJJ7wevHoteXitJc9DDwNv",
        "_type": "entry",
        "_entry": "2YlEGKqhO4mqRqEwQexeqRI8Jfu"
      }
    }
  ],
